        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Trimline is a legacy treadmill brand in the US: the Hebb-built
          machines have not been made for years, and owning one is now about parts, manuals and
          sensible limits.</strong> Wear parts such as belts and drive belts are still easy to find;
          electronics, rollers and incline motors often are not, so an electronic fault is the
          likeliest end of an old Trimline.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep a working one maintained, buy a used one only cheaply and after seeing it run, and stop
          spending when repairs approach the cost of a modern machine. When it is time to replace it,
